/*--------------------------------------------

TEST: a thin prism (base up) combined with a converging thin lens - a small
demonstration/regression system for the prism element, showing:
 - the wedge glyph rendered at the prism's position
 - the prism's constant angular deviation shifting the image sideways
   without changing where it forms or the system's magnification
 - correct combination with an ordinary lens elsewhere in the system

Dimensions match thin-lens-positive.lens's scale/convention (object at
z=-0.3, h=0.1, lens height=0.5/aperture=0.25) rather than a physically
realistic mm scale, for visual consistency with the other thin lens
examples.

----------------------------------------------*/

